    "title": "Justin Bieber’s Coachella set list may have been leaked by 'Love Island’ star",
    "text": "Justin Bieber gave Beliebers (yes, we're still saying that in 2026) a taste of what to expect at Coachella 2026 by performing surprise, invite-only shows at The Roxy and The Troubadour in Los Angeles over the past two weeks.Bieber exclusively sang songs from \"SWAG,\" his Grammy-nominated album from last July, and \"SWAG II,\" its surprise counterpart released last September. For that reason, the working assumption has been that Bieber's headlining Coachella set would be similar to his warm-up shows.Well, \"Love Island USA\" star Nic Vansteenberghe might have just leaked Bieber's Coachella headlining set list on Threads.LOS ANGELES, CALIFORNIA - FEBRUARY 01: Justin Bieber performs onstage during the 68th GRAMMY Awards at Crypto.com Arena on February 01, 2026 in Los An...Vansteenberghe posted \"Justin Bieber's song list\" with the disclaimer, \"The rumor going around town.\" The purported set list looks like this: \"Sorry\"\"With You\"\"So Sick\"\"Favorite Girl\" \"One Less Lonely Girl\"\"Baby\"\"I'm the One\"\"All That Matters\"\"Beauty and a Beat\"\"Where R U Now\"\"Daisies\"\"Yukon\"\"Devotion\"\"Love Song\"\"I Do\"\"Speed Demon\"Bieber reposted Vansteenberghe's viral \"Mommy? Mamacita\" scene with Huda Mustafa on \"Love Island USA\" Season 7 last summer. Vansteenberghe and Olandria Carthen were fan favorites and finished as runners-up. \"I just saw my face on his Instagram, and I know his new album dropped, too,\" Vansteenberghe told Decider last July. \"Good things for JB. I love that he did that.\" When alerted that Bieber used the clip to help promote \"SWAG,\" Vansteenberghe said, \"Hell yeah. JB, I want to go to your concert.\"Fans will find out whether Vansteenberghe had real intel, which is plausible now that he is well-connected in Hollywood, or was just guessing like the rest of us when Bieber stages the most significant concert of his career this weekend.Bieber will make his Coachella headlining debut on Saturday, April 11, and headline again on Saturday, April 18. Other than his invite-only L.A. shows, the generational pop star most recently performed at the 2026 Grammys on Feb. 1. Bieber earned high praise for his stripped-back, looped rendition of \"Yukon,\" his standout pop/R&B song from \"SWAG.\"Bieber also live-streamed on Twitch throughout October and December, including everything from his Coachella rehearsals and casual jam sessions to a special performance of \"Purpose\" to celebrate the album's 10th anniversary.",
